# 3. Scale Up Infrastructure

## New Components Added

### 1. Additional Load Balancer (HAproxy cluster)
We add a second load balancer to form a cluster with the first one.

**Why:**
- Removes Single Point of Failure (SPOF)
- Provides high availability
- If one load balancer fails, the other continues serving traffic

---

### 2. Separation of Components into Different Servers

#### Web Server (Nginx)
Handles HTTP/HTTPS requests and serves static content.

**Why:**
- Improves performance
- Allows independent scaling

---

#### Application Server
Executes application logic and processes dynamic requests.

**Why:**
- Separates logic from request handling
- Easier to maintain and scale independently

---

#### Database Server (MySQL)
Stores and manages application data.

**Why:**
- Dedicated resources for database operations
- Improves performance and reliability

---

### 3. Additional Server

Used to host one of the separated components (web/app/db).

**Why:**
- Enables distribution of workload
- Improves scalability and fault tolerance

---

## Benefits of This Architecture

- Better scalability (each layer can scale independently)
- Improved fault tolerance
- Clear separation of concerns
- Easier maintenance and upgrades
